    {
      "page": 25,
      "start": 1006,
      "end": 1048,
      "text": "REASONS FOR DENYING THE WRIT OF CERTIORARI",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "page": 25,
      "start": 1049,
      "end": 1142,
      "text": "I. THE THIRD CIRCUIT’S UNPUBLISHED OPINION REFLECTS THE FACTBOUND APPLICATION OF SETTLED LAW",
      "level": 2
    },
    {
      "page": 27,
      "start": 1229,
      "end": 1290,
      "text": "II. THERE IS NO CIRCUIT SPLIT WARRANTING THIS COURT’S REVIEW",
      "level": 2
    },
    {
      "page": 27,
      "start": 1291,
      "end": 1443,
      "text": "A. The alleged circuit split is illusory because the outcome of the cases is the same when grouped according to the basis of federal-court jurisdiction",
      "level": 3
    },
    {
      "page": 30,
      "start": 817,
      "end": 985,
      "text": "B. The circuit split claimed by Petitioner is also illusory because the specific terms of the various state statutes being applied differ in outcome-determinative ways.",
      "level": 3
    },
    {
      "page": 33,
      "start": 1251,
      "end": 1294,
      "text": "III. THE THIRD CIRCUIT’S RULING IS CORRECT",
      "level": 2
    },
    {
      "page": 39,
      "start": 869,
      "end": 916,
      "text": "IV. THIS CASE IS THE WRONG VEHICLE FOR REVIEW",
      "level": 2
    },
    {
      "page": 40,
      "start": 190,
      "end": 200,
      "text": "CONCLUSION",
      "level": 1
    }
